1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 95th generation. 466 to 540. Son of Qi (齐).
2 CONT
2 CONT An Augur in the Imperial Academy (祭酒太守) during the Northern and Southern Dynasties (南北朝).
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Madam Zhan (詹氏). Had 4 sons - Rui Yi (瑞仪), Duan Yi (端仪), Xiang Yi (祥仪) and Li Yi (礼仪).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 九十五世。公元466 - 公元540。齐之子, 端仪之父。
2 CONT
2 CONT 官至祭酒太守。
2 CONT
2 CONT 配詹氏, 生四子 - 瑞仪, 端仪, 祥仪, 礼仪。
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT NB - There are some discrepancies in the records. An internet genealogy record on Huang Yuan Fang (黄元方 - 百度百科) shows that Qi (齐) and Xi (西) were brothers. According to our Family Genealogy Book, Wen Ming Zu Jia Pu (文明祖家谱), Xi was 
2 CONC the son of Qi, but there was nothing written about Xi. Another Wong Genealogy Book, the Taishan Huang Shi Zu Pu (台山黄氏族谱), also recorded Gui Lin (贵林) as the son of Qi. I have therefore adopted the genealogy records of Huang Yuan Fa
2 CONC ng and the Taishan Huang Shi Zu Pu that Gui Lin was the son of Qi. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES (资料来源) -
