1 NAME Ju Zheng /HUANG 黄/
2 GIVN Ju Zheng
2 _MARNM HUANG 黄
1 NAME HUANG Ju Zheng, WONG Geoi Zing, 居政,111,105,1世
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1125
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1213
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 111th generation. 1125 to 1213. Eldest son of Cheng Luo (Cing Lok) (澄洛). Also known as Shi Bao (Sai Bou) (世保-諱), Wan Dan (Man Daam) (万石-字), Yin Zhai (Jan Zaai) (寅斋-号) and You (Jau) (由). Originally resided in Hantou
2 CONC  Street (涵頭街), Putian (莆田), Fujian province (福建省). He lived during the reigns of Emperor Gaozong (高宗), Xiaozong (孝宗) and Ninzong (宁宗).
2 CONT
2 CONT Achieved distinction of Top Scholar (Zong Jyun Kap Dai) (状元及第) in 1175 during the late Southern Song (Naam Sung Hau Kei) (南宋后期) Dynasty. Appointed initially as Magistrate in Mianzhou (Gam Zau Zi Zau 绵州知州) (during Southern Song Dyn
2 CONC asty, this was part of Chengdu prefecture 成都府,  Sichuan). He held several positions (Shi Bu Shi Lang, Si Bou Si Long, 使部侍郎; Xing Bou Shang Shu, Jing Bou Soeng Syu, 刑部尚书) and was later appointed a Grand Secretary of the Tianzhang P
2 CONC avilion (Tian Zhang Ge Zhi Xue Shi, Tin Zoeng Gok Zik Hok Si,天章阁直学士.  He was then transferred to the position of Grand Canal Transport Commissioner and held the rank of Zhongfeng Dafu (中奉大夫) and Eastern Zhejiang Inspection Commiss
2 CONC ioner (Zhe Dong An Fu Shi, Zit Dung On Fu Si, 浙东按撫使) during the reign of Song Xiao Zong (Sung Haau Zung) (宋孝宗). Later, he retired due to political disagreement and was posted to Yingzhou (Jing Zau Fu Zi Fu, 英州府知府) in Guangdong Pro
2 CONC vince, Nanxiong Prefecture, Baochang County, Zhuji Alley (Gwong Dung Naam Hung Fu Bou Coeng Jyun Zyu Gei Hong, 广东南雄府保昌县珠玑巷) and started his lineage from there. His eldest son Yuan Shen (源深) moved further south to Du Ruan, Xinhui (
2 CONC 杜阮, 新会).
2 CONT
2 CONT Regarded as the 1st ancestor of the Zhuji line (Zyu Gei Paai) (珠玑派) whose descendants are now mainly found in Guangzhou (Gwong Zau) (广州), Foshan (Fat Saan) (佛山), Jiangmen (Gong Mun) (江门), Kaiping (Hoi Ping) (开平), Panyu (Pun Jyu) (
2 CONC 番禺), Shunde (Seon Dak) (顺德), Taishan (Toi Saan) (台山), Shuibu (Seoi Bou) (水步) and Xinhui (San Wui) (新会). His lineage is also more widely known as Gangzhou line (冈州派) - Gangzhou is the old name for Xinhui (新会).
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife, Madam Wu (Mou Si) (巫氏) , bore him 3 sons - Yuan Shen (Jyun Sam) (源深), Yuan Fu (Jyun Fu) (源辅) and Yuan Zan (Jyun Zaan) (源赞). In the Huang Shi Zong Qin website (Wong Si Zung Can Mong) (黄氏宗亲网), a 2nd son is listed  as Yuan 
2 CONC Da (Jyun Daai) (源大) but he is not listed in our Family Genealogy Book (Man Ming Zou Gaa Pou) (文明祖家谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT According to my Family Genealogy Book, Wen Ming Zu Jia Pu (Man Ming Zou Gaa Pou) (文明祖家谱), he and his wife were buried in Xinhui (San Wui) (新会), Gu Gang Zhou (Gu Gong Zau) (古岗州), Heng Tang (Waang Tong) (横塘). The gravesite is called
2 CONC  Xi Niu Wang Yue (Sai Ngau Mong Jyut) (犀牛望月) because of the landscape around it. 
2 CONT
2 CONT An internet source mentioned that he was buried in Wu County, Guang Fu Li, Mt. Dengwei's middle peak, Northeast, Huang Ancestral Burial Site (Ng Jyun Gwong Fuk Lei Dang Wai Saan Zung Fung Dung Bak Wong Si Zou Fan) (吴县光福里邓尉山中峰东北黄氏祖
2 CONC 坟). His shrine is in Heng Tang (Waang Tong) (横塘), Shuibu (Seoi Bou) (水步) in Taishan (Toi Saan) (台山).
2 CONT
2 CONT Wu County is actually in Suzhou (Sou Zau) (苏州). Having regard to the fact that Ju Zheng actually settled in Zhuji Alley in Guangdong, it is more likely that he was buried in the area described by my Family Genealogy Book. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Update (March 2026): Based on the inscription around the Heng Tang (横塘) tombsite, and confirmation from  Dun He Tang Huang Wu Cun Zu Pu, Ju Zheng's original tomb was located outside the Song City Eastern Gate of Nanxiong at a hill
2 CONC  called Da Jing Tou (大进头). Its exact location was lost due to political turmoil. The Heng Tang memorial tomb (Yi Guan Zhong 衣冠冢 - his hat and official attire was buried here) was erected by his descendants to allow future descenda
2 CONC nts to pay their respect. This was last refurbished during Qing Dynasty Tongzhi 12th year.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1924, a Huang Clan Shrine (Wong Si Daai Zung Ci) (黄氏大宗词) was built in Zheng Shi Road, Taishan City (Toi Sing Zing Si Gaai) (台城正市街) to commemorate him. Based on information provided by Huang Bing Fu, from Huang Wu Cun (黄屋村) line
2 CONC age, this Clan Shrine was originally built for Juzheng's  great grandson Ruigu (锐固). Ruigu was the first Huang descendant who moved to Taishan area. Taishan's old name is Xinning (新宁). A school in Juzheng's name was also establish
2 CONC ed there in 1930. The school is no longer there but the Clan hall remains as a landmark. The building now serves as the office of Ju Zheng Yue Bao (Geoi Zing Jyut Bou) (居正月報), a monthly bulletin that reports on the Huang clan acti
2 CONC vities in China and overseas.
2 CONT
2 CONT His 17th generation descendant, Huang Shi Jun (Wong Si Zeon) (黄士俊), a Top Scholar (Zhuang Yuan Ji Di) (Zong Jyun Kap Dai) (状元及第) and an Imperial Court Official (Li Bu Shang Shu, Lai Bou Soeng Syu,礼部尚书) during the end-Ming (Ming Mu
2 CONC t) (明末) period, wrote a poem that is being used by the Yin Long Wong Clan as a reference to adopt the generation characters for their descendants. The poem  reads as follows:- Sheng Di Qi Wen Ming, Dao De Zun Chao Ting, Shi Chuan 
2 CONC Li Yi Zhong, Yi Si Zhen Jia Sheng; Sing Dai Kai Man Ming, Dou Dak Zyun Ciu Ting, Sai Cyun Lai Ji Zung, Jik Zi Zan Gaa Sing; 圣帝启文明, 道德尊朝廷; 世传礼义重, 奕祀振家声.
2 CONT
2 CONT NB - Ju Zheng's birth and death dates and the date he achieved the Top Scholar status are based on the records in the Taishan Huang Clan Yin Long Genealogy Book (Toi Saan Wong Si Jan Lung Zuk Pou) (台山黄氏隐龙族谱). An internet source in
2 CONC dicated that he was born in 1150 and died in 1225 and he became a Top Scholar in 1181. These dates are not used because, according  to the Taishan Huang Clan Yin Long Genealogy Book, Ju Zheng's son, Yuan Shen (源深), was born in 114
2 CONC 9 and became a Scholar in 1181. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 111世。公元1125 - 公元1213。澄洛公之长子, 源深公之父。諱世保, 字万石, 号寅斋。又名黄由。原居福建莆田县涵头街。
2 CONT
2 CONT 宋孝宗癸末, 胡虏数侵, 南渡中兴。祖积学, 应宋淳熙甲辰进士, 状元及第 (公元1175)。历任锦州知州, 英州府知府。擢吏部侍郎, 累官刑部尚书, 兼天章阁直学士。浙东按撫使, 卒赠少师, 乃遗命不迁之始祖。
2 CONT
2 CONT 妣巫氏, 诰封夫人, 生三子, 曰源深, 源辅, 迁天河横江, 源赞, 迁龙江崖山。
2 CONT
2 CONT 宋祐年间, 移迁广东, 南雄府保昌县, 珠玑巷居住。
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES (资料来源) -
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Wen Ming Zu Jia Pu (文明祖家谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Taishan Huang Shi Yin Long Zu Pu (台山黄氏隐龙族谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Huang Shi Ying Zuo Fang Yuan Qu Wu Hao Zhi Pu (黄氏英佐房园趣无号支谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. 黄元方 (280 - 375).
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. 黄氏宗亲网 - 广东黄氏.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. www.cnts.gov.cn (中国.台山政府网).
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.  Visits to the Huang Clan Shrine in Taishan City in November 2017 and March 2019.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. Dun He Tang Huang Shi Zu Pu (敦和堂黄氏族谱) - Huang Wu Cun, Chikan, Kaiping (黄屋村, 赤坎, 开平).
