1 NAME HUANG Guo Tai, WONG Gwok Taai, 黄国泰, 113,107, 3世
1 NAME 国泰 /黄/
2 GIVN 国泰
2 SURN 黄
1 SEX M
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 113th generation. Approximately 1154 to 1214. 2nd son of Yuan Shen (Jyun Sam) (源深). Also known as Chen Sheng (San Saang) (臣省-諱) and An Min (Ngon Man)) (安民-号).
2 CONT
2 CONT A Scholar (Zeon Si) (进士) and Magistrate of Ding Yuan District (Naam Ging Ding Jyun Jyun Zi Jyun) (南京定远县知县) in Nanjing (Naam Ging) (南京). Lived during the late Song (Sung Hau Kei) (宋后期) period and the Yuan (Jyun) (元) Dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Built the Yiai Shrine (Wai Oi Ci)) (遗爱祠) before retiring from official life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 4 wives - Madam Feng (Fung Si) (冯氏), Madam Hu (Wu Si) (胡氏), Madam Peng (Paang Si) (彭氏) and Madam Ke (O Si) (柯氏). Had 10 sons - Wen Guang (Man Gwong)) (文光), Wen Hui (Man Fai) (文辉), Wen Rao (Man Jiu) (文饒), Chao Xian (Ciu Hin
2 CONC ) (朝顯), Chao Wei (Ciu Wai) (朝威), Chao Yu (Ciu Juk) (朝玉), Chao Yong (Ciu Jung) (朝用), Chao Ying (Ciu Jing) (朝英), Chao Da (Ciu Daai) (朝大) and Chao Xi (Ciu Saai) (朝玺). The first 3 sons were born by Madam Feng.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was buried in Ping Ling Na Lai Shan (Ping Ling Naa Loi Saan) (平岭那来山), commonly known as Fu Yun Yong Yue (Fau Wan Jung Jyut) (浮云拥月), now under He Shan Gong He Zhen (Hok Saan Gung Wo Zan) (鹤山共和镇). In October 2019, his 1st wife Ma
2 CONC dam Feng's grave was re-sited next to his grave.
2 CONT
2 CONT He and his eldest brother, Guo Zong (Gwok Zung) (国宗), were credited for expanding and spreading the Huang (Wong) (黄) lineage.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 113世。约公元1154 - 约公元1214之间。源深公之次子, 朝威公之父。諱臣省, 号安民。
2 CONT
2 CONT 宋贡乡进士。任南京定远县知县。有遗爱祠。解组致仕。
2 CONT
2 CONT 配冯氏, 生子三人 - 曰文光, 文辉, 文饒。由古冈迁杜阮, 又娶胡, 彭柯三氏, 共生七子, 曰朝显, 朝威, 朝玉, 朝用, 朝英, 朝大, 朝玺。
2 CONT
2 CONT 由古冈迁文章若水, 朝威由古冈迁回南雄, 此復迁回南雄之始。
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES (资料来源) -
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Wen Ming Zu Jia Pu (文明祖家谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Taishan Huang Shi Yin Long Zu Pu (台山黄氏隐龙族谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Huang Shi Ying Zuo Fang Yuan Qu Wu Hao Zhi Pu (黄氏英佐房园趣无号支谱). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. 黄氏宗亲网 - 广东黄氏.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. 黄元方 - 百度百科.
