1 NAME 隱龍 字:慈庇 /黄/ 116,110,6,1世
2 GIVN 隱龍 字:慈庇
2 SURN 黄
2 NSFX 116,110,6,1世
2 NICK 王隱龍
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1223
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1311
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 116th generation. 1223 to 1311. Eldest son of Shu Li (Suk Lai) (叔礼). Also Known as Wen Guang (Man Gwong) (文光), Chen Ji (San Gei) (臣姬), Yun Cong (Wan Cung) (云从-諱), Ci Bi (Ci Bei) (慈庇-号) and Qian An (Cim Am) (潜庵-别字).
2 CONT
2 CONT A Scholar (Zeon Si) (进士-1253) and Magistrate of Guilin (Gwai Lam Zi Zau) (桂林知州) during the late Song (Sung Hau Kei) (宋后期) and Yuan (Jyun) (元) Dynasties.
2 CONT
2 CONT Had 3 wives, Madam Zhen (Jan Si) (甄氏), Madam Ou (Au Si) (区氏) and Madam Feng (Fung Si) (冯氏), and 7 sons - Song Wu (Cung Wu) (松坞),  Zhu An (Zuk Am) (竹庵-諱),  Mei Ye (Mui Je) (梅野), Yuan Chang (Jyun Coeng) (源长), Yuan Hong  (Jyun Wang) 
2 CONC (源宏), Yuan Liang (Jyun Loeng) (源谅) and Yuan Guang (Jyun Gwong) (源广). Mother of the first two sons was Madam Zhen. Third son, Mei Ye, was born by Madam Ou. The last 4 sons were born by Madam Feng.
2 CONT
2 CONT Settled in Dong Kou (Dung Hau) (洞口) from Nan Xiong (Naam Hung) (南雄) in 1252 and established the first generation of his lineage from there. His shrine is located there. Next to it is the shrine of his eldest Great Great Grandson, 
2 CONC De Ren (Dak Jan) (德仁). Renovation of the complex started on 28 December 2012 and took exactly one year to complete.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Dong Kou, his descendants have branched out and established their footings in more than 230 villages. Many have also settled overseas. The number of descendants from his lineage has now exceeded 200,000.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 116世。公元1223 - 公元1311。叔礼公之长子。諱云从, 号慈庇, 别字潜庵, 别名文光, 臣姬。
2 CONT
2 CONT 公元1253登宋进士。
2 CONT
2 CONT 妣甄氏, 生二子曰, 松坞, 竹庵。妾区氏, 生子曰梅野, 二妾冯氏, 生四子曰, 源长, 源宏, 源凉, 源广。
2 CONT
2 CONT 隐龙公为洞口开基之始祖。
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES (资料来源) -
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Wen Ming Zu Jia Pu (文明祖家谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Taishan Huang Shi Yin Long Zu Pu (台山黄氏隐龙族谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Huang Shi Ying Zuo Fang Yuan Qu Wu Hao Zhi Pu (黄氏英佐房园趣无号支谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Visits to Yin Long and De Ren shrines in November 2017, March 2019 and 22 October 2023.
