1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 119th generation. 1298 to 1383. Eldest son of Chao Xuan (Ciu Syun) (朝选). Also known as Hui Xuan (Wai Hin) (惠轩-号). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Magistrate of Luorong District (Lok Jung Jyun Zi Jyun) (洛溶县知县) during the late Yuan (Jyun Hau Kei) (元后期) and early Ming  (Ming Co) (明初) Dynasties.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dutiful and diligent, he was widely acclaimed for reclaiming 52 qing (King) (顷) of farmland, building the ancestral shrine and bequeathing 5 qing (顷) of land as endowment for ancestor worship. The remaining land was divided equall
2 CONC y among his four sons after his death. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Had 3 wives - Madam Kuang (Kwong Si) (邝氏), Madam Yu (Jyu Si) (余氏) and Madam Li (Lei Si) (李氏). Had 4 sons - De Ren (Dak Jan) (德仁), De Yi (Dak Ji) (德义), De Li (Dak Lai) (德礼) and De Zhi (Dak Zi) (德智-諱). 4th son, De Zhi, was mothered 
2 CONC by Madam Yu and given to his younger brother, Li Zhi (Lei Zik) (理直), to continue his lineage. Madam Li was childless.
2 CONT
2 CONT The shrine of his eldest son, De Ren, is located beside that of Yin Long (Jan Lung) (隐龙), his Great Grandfather, in Dong Kou (Dung Hau) (洞口).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 119世。公元1298 - 公元1383。朝选公之长子。諱里正, 号惠轩。
2 CONT
2 CONT 任洛溶县知县, 增置田塘五十二顷, 设立祠堂, 除田五顷, 永为烝嘗。
2 CONT
2 CONT 淑配邝氏, 生三子曰, 德仁, 德义, 德礼。继娶余氏, 德智公是妣所生也。又继娶李氏, 无子。
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES (资料来源) -
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Wen Ming Zu Jia Pu (文明祖家谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Taishan Huang Shi Yin Long Zu Pu (台山黄氏隐龙族谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Huang Shi Ying Zuo Fang Yuan Qu Wu Hao Zhi Pu (黄氏英佐房园趣无号支谱). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Visits to Yin Long and De Ren shrines in November 2017, March 2019 and 23 October 2023 (重阳节).
