1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 131st generation.Lived from 1690 to 1762.Eldest Son Of Erqi(而啟)and Madam Chen(陈氏).Also known as Anli(字-安立)and Xianping(号-顯平)
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Langxi Taishan during the early Qing Dynasty,during Rongying’s childhood,the average livelihood of the average taishan citizen was poor due to china having come out of decades of destructive civil war and the destruction o
2 CONC f the Ming Dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Not wanting to live a poor life,Rongying became one of the first chinese to migrate out of Taishan in 1707 and sailed for a long period of time before finally reaching the Island Of Bangka.Being one of the first chinese to reach b
2 CONC angka,rongying had a lot of business opportunities and decided to start a tin mining business,a new practice recently started by the VOC
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1713,after having secured his business,he returned to taishan to give back the money he had borrowed from his relatives and married Madam Li(李氏)and bore him a son Huakui(華逵).
2 CONT
2 CONT During the time of rongying,bangka was mostly an empty and quiet island,the village rongying selected to settle known as Belinyu had less than 1,000 residents spread over a area of 100 square km who were mostly miners.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rongying left his son and wife in langxi in the care of relatives,and traveled back to bangka.In 1722,the VOC reached an agreement with the Palembang Sultanate which granted them rights over the tin minings in Bangka.Using this op
2 CONC portunity,Rongying negotiated with the VOC for a majority of the tin mines in Bangka.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1727,Rongying eventually became the first dominant tin mine owner of bangka,this granted him immense power and influence over the rest of the tin mines in bangka as well as favorable bargaining positions with the VOC.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1733,the brought his wife and son to bangka,after his son had reached adulthood.In 1742,rongying was made one of the first Luitenant Der Chinezen of the island.He frequently returned to taishan to donate money and help the live
2 CONC lihoods of his relatives.In 1750,he was raised to the rank of Kaptein Titulair Der Chinezen highlighting the increasing chinese role in bangka.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1753,Rongying retired from public life as by then his son had reached the rank of Luitenant Der Chinezen.In 1762,Rongying died at at the age of 72,and was brought back and given a proper burial in Langxi the village he grew up 
2 CONC according to his wishes.The Dutch raised his rank posthumously to Kaptein Der Chinezen as respect for his hardwork and diligence in setting up one of the first’s chinese run tine mines in Bangka.At his death,Rongying was arguably 
2 CONC the richest chinese in bangka and one of the richest in the dutch east indies
