2 DATE 1745
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1814
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 133rd generation. 1745 to 1815. Only son of Fu Xue (Fu Hok) (富学). Also known as Yuan Si (Jyun Si) (源思-諱) and Da Cai (Daat Coi) (达才-号). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born into a poor family. Was only 9 years old when his father died. Grew up under very harsh conditions but managed to start a lintel making business during the Qing (Cing) (清) Dynasty. His fortune improved and his descendants wer
2 CONC e able to benefit from the growing prosperity for subsequent decades.
2 CONT
2 CONT He laid the foundation for a set of family rules (under the name of Ji Qing Tang, Zik Hing Tong, 积庆堂) to help family members with the cost of participating in public examinations and to encourage them to improve themselves. Reward
2 CONC s were also given for longevity. The rewards for excelling in examinations were, in fact, continued in the Singapore branch (Tian Chi Tang, Tin Ci Tong, 天池堂) up to the 1970s.
2 CONT
2 CONT Had 3 wives, Madam Chen (Can Si) (陈氏), Madam Zhu (Zyu SI) (朱氏) and Madam Li (Lei Si) (李氏), and 4 sons - Xing Zun (Hang Zyun) (杏尊), Peng Zun (Paang Zyun) (鹏尊-字), Zan Zun (Zaan Zyun) (瓒尊) and Qi Zun (Kei Zyun) (琪尊). The first two so
2 CONC ns were born by Madam Chen while the remaining 2 sons were born by Madam Zhu and Madam Li respectively.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was buried together with Madam Chen near Yanjingcun (Ngaan Geng Cyun) (眼镜村). The grave site is perched on top of  a very steep hill (Song Zi Ling, Cung Zai Ling, 松仔岭) with a commanding view of the village and its surroundings. 
2 CONC According to geomancy, the topography of the grave site and the surrounding landscape resembles a bell being supported by a beam (Waang Loeng Diu Zung) (横樑吊钟). The bell is where the grave is located. It is believed to have very go
2 CONC od feng shui (fung seoi) (风水). The orientation of the grave was determined to harness the full blessings of the feng shui to benefit the descendants. It is recorded in the Wen Ming Zu Jia Pu (文明祖家谱) that the orientation of the gra
2 CONC ve must not be altered.
2 CONT
2 CONT His gravesite is one of the 4 gravesites where our ancestors in Yanjingcun were buried. The other three are Rat Hill (Shu Shan, Syu Saan, 鼠山), where Fu Xue was buried; Wang Jiang Shi (Mong Gong Si, 望江狮), where Fu Xue's wife (Madam
2 CONC  Zhao, Ziu Si, 赵氏) was buried; and Tiger Hill (Hu Shan, Fu Saan, 虎山), where Wong Ah Fook's mother (Madam Mai, Mak Si, 麦氏) was buried. In 2020, Madam Mai's remains were re-buried next to Fu Hok's grave because Tiger Hill was flatte
2 CONC ned for development.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 133世。公元1745 - 公元1815。富学翁之子也。諱源思, 字宏讓, 号达才。
2 CONT
2 CONT 居家寒微出身劳碌九岁失怙上无则友之兄下无祇恭之弟形单影只而能克勤克俭手创门楣基业定始於此焉。
2 CONT
2 CONT 妣陈氏, 生子二人曰, 靈辅(杏尊), 狗(鹏尊)。妾朱氏, 生子一人曰四(瓒尊)。又妾李氏, 生子一人曰癸穏(琪尊)。
2 CONT
2 CONT 讓祖妣合葬之坟自后道光二十八年适有江西廖桂馨老师到来看准此向登时贺曰乃是福人葬福山其中必有神人所使乃得其向云云真真匪余所思也故修於谱祈为后裔者慎勿听时师搅扰焉可也。
2 CONT
2 CONT 翁遗落基业嗣后守其成者积小增大矢慎矢公数十余年於兹矣今虽非丰享裕大而用之不穷以视夫昔日迁徒之余艰难险阻之备嘗者则有间矣而为子若孙者徒拥其赀不为继志述事之举其有负于我。
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES (资料来源) -
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Wen Ming Zu Jia Pu (文明祖家谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Taishan Huang Shi Yin Long Zu Pu (台山黄氏隐龙族谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Huang Shi Ying Zuo Fang Yuan Qu Wu Hao Zhi Pu (黄氏英佐房园趣无号支谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Grave site visit on 14 March 2019.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. https://www.iseas.edu.sg/wp-content/uploads/2015/07/Wong_Ah_Fook_Collection - A_Descriptive_Catalogue_website.pdf
