1 NAME Majoor Der Chinezen Van Bangka Huang Yi Zhong,Bong Jit Tjhong,Wong Jik Zung, 黄奕忠, 135, 129, 25世 /HUÁNG 黃/
2 GIVN Majoor Der Chinezen Van Bangka Huang Yi Zhong,Bong Jit Tjhong,Wong Jik Zung, 黄奕忠, 135, 129, 25世
2 _MARNM HUÁNG 黃
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1797
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1891
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 135th generation.Lived from 1797-1891.Son of Daneng(達能)and Madam Lei(雷氏).Also known as Guofu(字-国富)and Pingan(号-平安)
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Langxi,Taishan during the Jiaqing era Of The Qing Dynasty to the powerful overseas chinese Huang Daneng(達能)at age 25,he married Madam Mei(梅氏)and had a son Shihao(世豪).Due to his father’s influence and financial security he 
2 CONC was able to learn about the ways about tin mining from the few europeans in china,a luxury not available to the masses.He took the Jinshi test in the 1820s and managed to secure a degree(進士)and a scholarship in the Qing Court
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1829,he migrated to bangka,dutch east indies with his father Daneng(達能) leaving his wife and son in the care of relatives,to join his grandfather who had already settled there since the late 1700s,he was able to secure a tin mi
2 CONC ne ownership through his father’s influences and was made Luitenant Der Chinezen in the 1830s.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1835,his son Shihao(世豪),who he had not seen for 6 years,traveled to bangka alone in search of his father and was able to find him with relative ease,during that period Yizhong had advanced and grown to be a top contender in the
2 CONC  tin mine business in Bangka.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1844,his father Daneng(達能)died in Bangka at the age of 78 due to an unknown illness and Yizhong brought him back to Langxi for a proper burial.in the mid 1840s,Yizhong was raised to the status of Kaptein Der Chinezen Van Bangka
2 CONC  due to his extraordinary abilities and prestige.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1852,using some of his excess money from his tin mine business,he created a diverse business of selling food,cooking needs and fossil fuels for his son who by then had matured.In 1859,Yizhong traveled to Batavia(capital of dutc
2 CONC h east indies)and managed to close a deal which made him the dominant tin mine owner in North Bangka.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1855,due to the severe unstability in China due to the opium wars and Qing’s mismanagement,Yizhong decided to create replica’s of his ancestor’s tablet to Huang Juzheng(25 generations seperation)and bring them to Bangka incase 
2 CONC the tablets in China would be destroyed by rebels,as well as a copy of the Langxi Wong Zupu which still survives as a copy till today.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1862,Yizhong bought a Qing Dynasty Official Positions to solidify his prestige as both a dominant chinese conglomerate in bangka and a talented scholar as well to ensure his mother would get a proper burial in Langxi.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1869,Yizhong retired from the business world but still retained his title of Kaptein Der Chinezen albeit with reduced responsibilities,as his son who was 44 by then had also risen to the rank of Kaptein Der Chinezen.
2 CONT
2 CONT He used his vast wealth to improve the lifelihoods of the tin mine workers working under him and was known for raising the pay of some of them who were in need of money or other emergency situations.
2 CONT
2 CONT Throughout his life,Yizhong had developed several close friendships with prominent dutch officials such as the Dutch Comissioner Of Bangka and the Dutch Governor General of the dutch east indies.He frequently returned to taishan d
2 CONC espite being in his advanced age during the Qingming festival to worship his father’s and ancestor’s tombs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Yizhong died in 1891,at the age of 94,in the large family home he had built in Belinyu.He was given a proper burial suited for someone of his high status,he was buried in either Bangka or back in Langxi.His Ancestral Tablet is sit
2 CONC uated in the House he built.
2 CONT
2 CONT The current photo displayed on his profile,is the last surviving photo of him which still survives to this day.
2 CONT
2 CONT 第一百三十五世祖
2 CONT (1797—1891）
2 CONT 字国富，号平安
2 CONT 达能公与雷氏太夫人次子
2 CONT
2 CONT 公生于清朝嘉庆年间，广东台山朗溪。父达能公乃南洋巨贾，家资丰饶，故公少时得习文识字，兼从留华西人处研习锡矿之术，此非常人所能及。及长，娶梅氏为妻，生子世豪。道光初年，公赴科举，中进士，获朝廷赐俸，显赫乡里。
2 CONT
2 CONT 道光九年（1829），公随父远渡南洋，至荷兰东印度邦加岛，投奔祖父基业。唯妻、子暂留故里。公凭父荫，购得锡矿，又因才德出众，约道光十年间授“雷珍兰”（Luitenant der Chinezen）之职，协理华社。
2 CONT
2 CONT 道光十五年（1835），子世豪独赴邦加寻父，终得团聚。时公经营有方，已为邦加锡业翘楚。道光二十四年（1844），达能公在邦加病逝，享年七十有八。公扶柩归葬台山朗溪，恪尽孝道。越数年，公晋为“甲必丹”（Kaptein der Chinezen van Bangka），统理邦加华务，声望日隆。
2 CONT
2 CONT 咸丰二年（1852），公以锡矿之利，助子世豪开拓米粮、炊具、燃料诸业，家业愈广。咸丰九年（1859），公亲赴巴达维亚，订约而取北大年锡矿专营之权，势倾一方。
2 CONT
2 CONT 然公心系故国文脉。时值鸦片战后，中原动荡，公恐祖祠碑牌罹难，遂于咸丰五年（1855）委人摹刻远祖黄居正公（相隔二十五世）神位碑，并抄录《台山朗溪黄氏族谱》一部，携至邦加保存。此谱副本存世至今，皆赖公之高瞻。
2 CONT
2 CONT 同治元年（1862），公捐纳清廷官衔，既荣母丧葬礼制，亦固其侨领兼儒臣之尊。至同治八年（1869），公年高隐退，甲必丹之衔仍留，实务付予世豪（时亦为甲必丹）。公秉性仁厚，常济矿工急困，薪饷优给，邦人感念。
2 CONT
2 CONT 公一生交游广阔，与邦加荷兰督辦、东印度总督等多有往还。暮年仍屡返台山祭扫，清明时节，舟车不顾耄耋。
2 CONT
2 CONT 光绪十七年（1891），公卒于邦加勿里洋家宅，享寿九十有四。葬仪依品秩而行，或云归葬朗溪祖茔，或云安息邦加。其墓葬於邦加或朗溪.神位在和玖公祠.
