1 NAME Majoor Der Chinezen Van Bangka Huang Shihao,Bong Sa Hao,Wong Sai Hou, 黄世豪, 136,130, 26世 /HUÁNG 黃/
2 GIVN Majoor Der Chinezen Van Bangka Huang Shihao,Bong Sa Hao,Wong Sai Hou, 黄世豪, 136,130, 26世
2 _MARNM HUÁNG 黃
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE AFT 1825
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1902
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 136th generation.Lived from 1825 to 1902.Only son of Yizhong(奕忠)and Madam Mei(梅氏).Also known as Beifo(諱-北佛)and Fushou(号-福寿)
2 CONT
2 CONT Shihao was born in the village of Langxi(朗溪)in the county of Taishan(台山)during the later years of the Qing Dynasty.at the age of 4 his father,Yizhong(奕忠)returned to Bangka after his father had sent for him who by then was already 
2 CONC an old man to continue the family business.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1835,Shihao went to bangka alone to find his father and discovered he had already garnered a substantial amount of wealth and political power in the 6 years he was gone.After reconnecting with his father,he returned to china to
2 CONC  continue his studies and earned the Jinshi(進士)degree in the 29th year of Emperor Daoguang(道光二十九年).In 1850,he married lady wu(伍夫人)who bore him 9 sons and 1 daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT During his time in china,as a jinshi degree holder he held numerous high ranking positions including,Prefect Of Taishan(台山府尹)in 1852,Minister Of Board Of Works(工部尚书) in 1855,Prefect of Guangdong(廣東府尹) in 1860 and Chief Official Of
2 CONC  The Court Of Judicial Affairs(大理寺卿) in 1865,he retired in 1866 and was honorably promoted to Chief Minister(卿士)for his hardwork and service over the years by Emperor Tongzhi.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his retirement from Qing officialdom,he returned to bangka due to the need for someone to suceed his father who was already old and weakening by then.Shihao started off as a small tin mine businessman in bangka but quickly r
2 CONC ose through the business,using his father’s vast wealth and resources to his advantage which earned him a promotion to Luitenant Der Chinezen in 1867.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the days of Shihao,the population of bangka was dominated mostly by chinese who were brought in from china by the dutch government to work as tin mine workers,Shihao often cared and looked out for the wellbeing of the miner
2 CONC s under him which earned him great support and appreciation from the miners who performed well under him.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1871,Shihao was raised to the rank of Kaptein Titulair Der Chinezen by the Dutch government to replace his father Yizhong who had by then gone into retirement but still held some minor responsibilities.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1876,he was fully promoted to the rank of Kaptein Der Chinezen to fully replace his father,by then he was one of the most powerful and wealthy chinese in bangka.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1882,Shihao was promoted to the rank of Majoor Titulair Der Chinezen to manage the activities of the chinese dominated tin mines,as a result of the rapid increase of chinese tin mine due to the deteriorating state of the Qing d
2 CONC ynasty during that time.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1889,7 years after his raising to the rank of Majoor Titulair Der Chinezen,Shihao fell gravely ill and was forced to temporarily relinquish his power and responsibilities to his eldest son Luitenant Titulair Der Chinezen Huang 
2 CONC Zhen Xiong(黄振雄) who was temporarily raised to the rank of Luitenant Der Chinezen.
2 CONT
2 CONT After recovering,Shihao decided to continue on with his duties,but by then his age had caught up with him and he began suffering frequent bouts of illness limiting his working capacity.He decided to continue to endure it for years
2 CONC ,in 1893,the dutch finally raised him to the highest rank of Majoor Der Chinezen highlighting his important role in bangka,but in 1895,his health had declined to such a state that he began suffering from frequent stress and headac
2 CONC hes which finally forced him to relinquish his responsibilities and power to his eldest son Kaptein Titulair Der Chinezen Huang Zhen Xiong.
2 CONT
2 CONT He retired to the home of his ancestors in bangka from 1895 onwards but his health still continued to deteriorate at a swift rate.By 1899,he was nearly almost bedridden due to his frail and weak state,he decided to return back to 
2 CONC Langxi one last time and was accompanied by all 9 of his sons.In Langxi he went to every ancestral temple his ancestor’s tablets were in as well as visiting and praying at all their graves.He had wanted to visit Putian(莆田)too but 
2 CONC his fast deteriorating health prevented him from doing so.
2 CONT
2 CONT After returning to Bangka,shihao was bedridden for the rest of his life and his appetite also started deteriorating.In 1902,shihao passed away peacefully at the age of 77 after enduring through 13 years of illness,immediately afte
2 CONC r his death,his eldest son Kaptein Der Chinezen Huang Zhen Xiong assumed full responsibilities over the activities of chinese tin mines in North Bangka and was temporarily raised to the rank of Majoor Titulair Der Chinezen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Shihao was buried in belinyu,the town on the island of Bangka in the Dutch East Indies,where his ancestor Kaptein Titulair Der Chinezen Huang Rongying(黄荣映)had first settled in.On his deathbed shihao had requested his grave not bea
2 CONC r any prominent insignias and markings that he was a high ranking colonial chinese officer which his sons obeyed.Immediately after his death,his eldest son ordered the making of his ancestral tablet which survives till today
