1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Mrs Cheong Pak Chow (nee Lydia Wong Yoke Lin) is the wife of former Director of Civil Aviation (Singapore), who later joined the International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO) in Montreal. Mrs Cheong is the gr
2 CONC anddaughter of entrepreneur Wong Ah Fook.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT CHEONG, Lydia Yoke Lin (nee Wong) 1928 - 2017 After 64 years of marriage and in her 89th year, Lydia, beloved wife of Cheong Pak Chow, loving sister of Yoke Lan (John) and Peter (Margaret), devoted mother to Peter (Amanda), Philom
2 CONC ena (Kuan Shin), Paul (Christina), Patricia, Patrick (Esther), Petronella, Pius (Kay) and Philip (Li-Hsien), and affectionate grandmother to Alexander (Alexandra), Natasha, Catherine, Lindsay, Kimberly (Rajiv), Olivia, Brendan, Je
2 CONC remy, Nicholas, Edwina (Mike), Darren and Connor, passed away peacefully in the presence of loved ones in Montreal on September 29, 2017. Lydia was born in Singapore in 1928 to Agnes Chan Ah Choy and Dato Wong Siew Qui, and was gr
2 CONC anddaughter of Wong Ah Fook. In 1975, Canada became her new home where she quickly developed admirable skills as a homemaker and excelled in the culinary arts. Dinner parties that she and Pak Chow hosted were coveted affairs. Her 
2 CONC passion in faith and religious convictions were central to her well lived life; visiting the Holy Land was one of its highlights. Lydia was a remarkable teacher of integrity and compassion to her children, and was always positive 
2 CONC in the face of adversity. She will be fondly remembered for her love of life's lighter side, her innate humility, candor and unassuming wit, and, her baffling propensity to win at Mah-jong and Dominoes. Lydia was dearly loved by a
2 CONC ll of us and will be sadly missed. Rest in peace and may perpetual light shine upon you. Family will receive condolences at Mount Royal Funeral Complex, 1297 chemin de la Forêt, Outremont, QC H2V 2P9, on Wednesday, October 4, 2017
2 CONC  from 5 p.m. to 9 p.m. Funeral service will be in the chapel of the funeral complex on Thursday, October 5, 2017 at 1 p.m. follow by a burial at Mount Royal Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of: Patricia Cheong; Patrick Cheong; Paul Cheong; Peter Cheong; Petronella Cheong; Philip Cheong; Philomena Cheong, (1954 - 2017) and Pius Cheong
2 CONT
