1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://eresources.nlb.gov.sg/newspapers/digitised/article/straitstimes19940125-1.2.52.3?qt=kwan,%20teet&q=KWAN%20teet
2 CONT
2 CONT from Pui ah
2 CONT l remember  reading in the newspaper about Michelle winning numerous  baking competitions despite having no formal culinary training.
2 CONT The prizes consisted  of numerous trips and Michelle proudly showed off of that she virtually travelled the world for free.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Peter LOH
2 CONT Just a little more information about Michelle 
2 CONT Her urn will be placed in the columbarium in Telok Ayer Chinese Methodist Church facing Keppel Golf Club 
2 CONT Many years ago, her eldest brother Dr. Kwan Teet Meng died of pancreatic cancer. He was a medical doctor and he knew his case was hopeless. He loved golf and had arranged his final resting place would be facing a golf course. 
2 CONT Meanwhile my parents were at Garden of Remembrance in Chua Chu Kang. I loved them dearly and found it difficult to visit them regularly I therefore arranged their urns to be next to Meng. 
2 CONT I then bought 3 additional double niches— one for myself and Michelle, one for Simon and wife ( hopefully they take it) and one for Mdm Kwan Mei Yee (Meng’s second daughter. 
